  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Verdict: the requirement is met.** I based this on the supplied excerpts of `src/config.rs` and `tests/configuration.rs`. I did not read the rest of either file.\n\n**User file (`UserConfig`, `src/config.rs`)**\n- `UserConfig` is a serde struct with `version: u32` and `authoring: Option<UserAuthoringConfig>`. It has `#[serde(deny_unknown_fields)]`. The root can therefore hold only `version` and the scoped feature tables, and unscoped feature keys are rejected.\n- `UserConfig::parse` uses `toml::from_str`. `validate` rejects any `version != 1`. `version` has no serde default, so a file without it is rejected.\n- `load_user_config` reads with `fs::read_to_string`, so input must be UTF-8.\n- `authoring` is `Option` with `default`. A file containing only `version = 1` is valid, and an absent section is `None`, which is distinct from an explicit `[authoring]`.\n- `to_toml` round-trips the struct. `skip_serializing_if` leaves out absent options.\n\n**Project file (`ProjectConfig`, `src/config.rs`)**\n- `ProjectConfig::from_book_toml` parses `book.toml` as a generic table and reads only the `habeas` key. It returns `Ok(None)` when `[habeas]` is absent and `Ok(Some(..))` when it is present, so absence is distinguishable from an empty or explicit section.\n- `ProjectConfig` has `deny_unknown_fields`, so a `version` key inside `[habeas]` is rejected. The user-file version is therefore not required, or even accepted, there.\n- `resolve_authoring` calls `from_book_toml`, so the project structure is checked on the real path.\n\n**Tests (`tests/configuration.rs`)**\n- `absent_and_minimal_configuration_are_distinct_and_read_only` is tagged `{test}requirements.configuration.structure`. It covers these cases:\n  - a missing user file gives `None` and is not created;\n  - a `version = 1`-only file loads with `authoring` as `None` and is left unmodified;\n  - serialization round-trips;\n  - `book.toml` without `[habeas]` gives `None`;\n  - an empty `[habeas]` gives `Some(ProjectConfig {})`;\n  - `[habeas]` with `version = 1` is an error.\n- `invalid_schema_and_feature_values_report_the_configuration_path` covers `version = 2`, `version = '1'`, an empty file (no version), and an unknown root key. These cover the version requirement and the \"only version and feature tables at the root\" rule. It is tagged for loading rather than structure, but it exercises the same code.\n\n**Minor gaps, none material**\n- There is no test for non-UTF-8 bytes. The behaviour follows from `read_to_string`.\n- There is no test of a concrete `[habeas.<feature>]` table, because no project feature tables are defined yet. `ProjectConfig` is empty, and authoring explicitly defines no project section.\n\nNo FIXME markers are involved.",
